# nr-tui-style: wiring for the new crate mixdog-tui-style (lead applies, then deletes this file)

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml  [workspace] members
Anchor: the line `"crates/mixdog-js",` in `members` (the list is not alphabetical). Add directly after it the line
    "crates/mixdog-tui-style",
(If nr-tui-termtext-width's line `"crates/mixdog-termtext",` is already there, put this one after it.)

## 2. native/core/Cargo.toml  [workspace.dependencies]
Anchor: the line `mixdog-js = { path = "crates/mixdog-js" }`. Add, in alphabetical place:
    mixdog-tui-style = { path = "crates/mixdog-tui-style" }
No new external crate: serde, serde_json and mixdog-js are already workspace dependencies. Cargo.lock gets one new
`[[package]] name = "mixdog-tui-style"` with dependencies mixdog-js, serde, serde_json (and mixdog-js again as a
dev-dependency, which Cargo.lock does not list twice).

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-tui-style/Cargo.toml
After the workspace hack is regenerated, add to [dependencies] the line every peer crate has:
    mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }
and list mixdog-tui-style in native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml if hakari does so for peers.

## 4. Nothing else
No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING change, no registration, no feature or environment switch. The crate is a library;
consumers (the markdown, highlight, widget and app crates of the node-removal track) add
`mixdog-tui-style = { workspace = true }` themselves.

## Not compiled (the task forbids cargo)
The whole crate was written without a compile. First things to run after wiring:
    cargo test --offline -p mixdog-tui-style
    node native/core/crates/mixdog-tui-style/tests/recorders/record-style.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --check native/core/crates/mixdog-tui-style/tests/goldens/style.json
    cargo test --offline -p mixdog-tui-style -- --ignored live_style
    cargo clippy --offline -p mixdog-tui-style --all-targets -- -D warnings
goldens/style.json was re-recorded by this task: the stored one had been recorded with every Ink level pinned to 3
(levels 1 and 2 were identical to 3), so it could not check the 16-colour and 256-colour downgrade.

## Interfaces added (for the tasks that consume them)
palette: Key (67 keys, Key::ALL, Key::name), BASE, THEMES (14 entries in display order), THEME_ALIASES, DEFAULT_THEME_ID.
theme: Color {Rgb, Transparent} with css(), Palette (Index<Key>), ThemeEntry, ThemeInfo, ThemeSelection, set_theme(id),
  get_theme_setting(), get_theme_version() (monotonic AtomicU64, the cache key of the markdown and highlight caches),
  list_themes(), current_palette(), theme_color(Key), osc_background_sequence(&str), terminal_background_sequence(&Palette),
  TURN_MARKER, AGENT_CALL_MARKER, AGENT_RESPONSE_MARKER, RESULT_GUTTER, RESULT_GUTTER_CONT. set_theme does not write OSC 11
  (the app writes terminal_background_sequence when it owns a terminal) and does not persist ui.theme (config/setTheme does).
figures: the eleven glyph constants of figures.mjs.
color: chalk level-3 codes (FG_CLOSE, BG_CLOSE, BOLD_OPEN/CLOSE, DIM, ITALIC, UNDERLINE, INVERSE, STRIKE, fg_rgb, bg_rgb),
  chalk_wrap(text, open, close) (chalk's applyStyle for one style), rgb_to_ansi256, Style, Styler (from_environment,
  process, paint, compose, rgb_sgr), strip_ansi, visible_width.
color_level: ColorEnvironment {vars, argv, windows_release, stream_is_terminal} with level() (chalk's supports-color) and
  from_process(stream_is_terminal, windows_release); ink_colorize(text, color, background, level) (Ink's colorize at a
  chalk level). The Windows build string (os.release()) and the terminal check are given by the caller because this crate
  has no Windows dependency: the widget painter passes them once.
bridge: StatuslineColors, normalize_statusline_ansi(text, &colors, reset), statusline_footer_identity_changed(args, last).
spinner_verbs: SPINNER_VERBS (187), SPINNER_FRAMES, SPINNER_MODE_OVERRIDE_VERBS, spinner_verb_for, spinner_verb_in,
  mode_override_verb. The choice needs no random source (a hash of the turn start and boundary index is the coin), so
  none is injected; the clock is an argument.
spinner_meta: build_spinner_meta (SpinnerMetaInput, SpinnerMeta, Serialize camelCase), spinner_thinking_parts/label,
  quiet_progress_parts/label, ThinkingParts, Quiet, QuietParts, is_reduced_motion(MIXDOG_REDUCED_MOTION value).
time_format: format_duration(ms, DurationOptions), format_elapsed(ms).

## Duplicates seen, left for their owners
mixdog-core-session/src/session/spinner.rs holds its own copy of the 187-verb pool and the pick; it can read
mixdog_tui_style::spinner_verbs once that crate may depend on this one (not done here: not a file of this task).
mixdog-core-agents quiet_progress.rs ports the quiet-state producer of quiet-progress.mjs; the display parts and label the
byline uses (quietProgressParts / quietProgressLabel) live in spinner_meta.rs because no Rust port of them existed.
